     "explanation": "Across the studies Buettner cites — including Adventist Health Study-2 and several denomination-agnostic cohort studies — regular **faith-community attendance adds between 4 and 14 years** of life expectancy. The mechanism is bundled: ritual provides downshift, community provides belonging, doctrine provides purpose, and shared meals provide built-in social structure. Purpose alone contributes ~7 years; faith stacks several Power 9 pillars at once.",
