     "explanation": "The 2007 NEJM analysis tracked roughly 12,000 Framingham residents over 32 years and found that **having a close friend who becomes obese raises your own obesity risk by approximately 57%** — larger than the effect of having an obese sibling (40%) or spouse (37%). The mechanism is unconscious behavioral and norm contagion: meal pacing, food choices, exercise expectations, and even what counts as a normal body shape spread through social networks. This is why choosing your Right Tribe is a longevity decision.",
