     "explanation": "The Albert Lea pilot (2009-2011) is one of the most-cited Blue Zones Project results: average life expectancy rose **+2.9 years**, municipal employee healthcare costs dropped **~40%**, and smoking rates fell over **30%**. The Buettner thesis is vindicated: when the **environment defaults to belonging, walking, and plant-eating**, individual willpower is no longer the limiting factor. This is why the Capstone plan includes a community layer, not just personal habits.",
